<%# The quiet fine print at the foot of every page — insurance and tax
    registration by default, but editable per organization under Quote
    Customization, so it may be anything they want.

    Newlines are honoured: the field is a textarea and organizations are
    expected to use several lines. `simple_format` is avoided because it wraps
    in <p> tags that carry their own margins into the footer; `<br>` keeps the
    lines tight. Escaped first — this is user-entered text.

    NOTE: this is repeated per page rather than pinned to the bottom of the
    sheet, so on a short document it floats up under the content, and a page
    that overflows inherits no footer at all. The fix is wkhtmltopdf's
    --footer-html, which needs a change to GenerateQuote/GenerateReceipt —
    tracked as a follow-up, see .sdd/ENG-11/mockups/NOTES.md. %>
<% footer_text = organization.quote_footer_text %>

<table class='pdf-footer'>
  <tr>
    <td>
      <% if footer_text.present? %>
        <%= h(footer_text).gsub(/\r?\n/, '<br>').html_safe %>
      <% end %>
    </td>
    <td><%= estimate.quote_display_address %></td>
  </tr>
</table>
